# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  MikuOS — what never goes in the repo.
#
#  Three rules, in order of how badly you do not want to get them wrong:
#    1. Nothing that can sign a build.
#    2. Nothing of HiBy's, Qualcomm's, Google's or anyone else's.
#    3. Nothing a clean checkout can rebuild for itself.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. Signing material ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Falcon Technix platform key IS the trust anchor of a MikuOS build. Anyone
# holding it can sign something the OS will treat as a platform app. It is not in
# this repo, it never will be, and these patterns exist so it cannot get here by
# accident.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.pk8
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
*.der
*.crt
keystore.properties
mikuos/signing/
tools/*.pk8
tools/*.pem
tools/*.keystore
miku_m500_private.key

# ── 2. Not ours to redistribute ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# 16GB of decompiled HiBy firmware and extracted stock apps. It is their code, it
# is 16GB, and one of those trees holds a live third-party private key.
m500-system-archive/
**/decompiled_vendor_software/
**/extracted_fs/
**/smali*/
**/jadx_sources/

# Third-party APKs: Spotify, Tidal, Qobuz, Deezer, Apple Music, Chrome, Signal,
# Telegram, Magisk, GApps. Ours to install, not ours to hand out.
mikuos-optional-apks/
mikuos/build/optional_apks/
mikuos/build/preloaded_apks/
mikuos/build/gapps_dl/
*.apk
*.apks
*.apk.idsig

# HiBy's own artwork, audio and boot media, pulled off the device.
miku-assets/hiby-extracted/
miku-assets/vendor-media/
mikuos/build/boot_voice/
mikuos/build/audio/

# ── 3. Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Partition images. 5GB each, produced by build_mikuos_super.sh from stock
# firmware you supply yourself.
*.img
*.img.gz
*.sparse
mikuos/out/
mikuos_system_build/
mikuos/gsi/

# Gradle, Android, Go
**/build/
**/.gradle/
**/.cxx/
**/.kotlin/
tools/gradle-*/
local.properties
.idea/
*.iml
mikuos/web-flasher/mikuos-flasher
mikuos/web-flasher/mikuos-web-flasher
mikuos/web-flasher/miku-web-flasher

# The Kotlin apps are their own repo: github.com/sworrl/MikuMusic
miku-player-kotlin/
m500-hardware-settings/

# Big prebuilt tooling. apktool and baksmali are upstream releases, fetch them.
tools/apktool.jar
tools/baksmali.jar
*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# ── Personal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Network configs hold PSKs and addressing. Ingest config holds a personal host.
# The library database is a listing of one person's music collection.
*.conf
!tools/rsync/rsyncd.conf
mikuos-dev-wifi.conf
tools/m500-sync.env
*.env
!*.env.example
library/library.db
library/*.csv
library/*.json
device-dumps/
crash-logs/

# ── Agent / editor scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.aider*
.cursor/
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# ── OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Reference art pulled off the internet. Fine to keep on a workstation, not ours
# to republish. The renders under miku_renders/ and themes/ are generated for this
# project and do ship.
miku-assets/online/
